 # Futureox Design development
+
+- The 2026-10-26 motion-continuity repair is recorded in [its evidence and remaining failures](../../../testing/verification-motion-continuity-20261025/README.md). Atomic layer import, exact background initialization, scoped cancellation and resource admission address reproduced transparency failures; retained-frame quality alone cannot establish timely object motion. The wide rational prefix candidate remains strictly opt-in. Real fast zoom and topology edit convergence still fail; do not call this a complete rendering fix.
 
 - The 2026-10-25 rendering pipeline increment is documented in [its scoped implementation and verification record](../../../testing/verification-render-pipeline-20261025/README.md). Keep exact source identities separate from transfer-cache LRU; subtree fragments share the existing program allowance and require precise invalidation. Cooperative cancellation preserves the physical request fence and never cancels edits/exports. Shared-memory availability, native transport, target GPU readback and whole-editor motion are distinct gates. Large exact retained filters and opaque batching keep their existing opt-in policy.
 
